        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R87-002', 'version' => '1.104.1', 'date' => '2026-11-06', 'title' => 'Personal assistant scope: the Organisations wizard (link, create, merge, derive people), the related companies of a vessel and the Contacts finder are now hers, and My leave (her own requests, leave periods to join, training, targets) and Support are back on her menu; everything else stays closed (no projects, money, no other people\'s HR data).', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R87-001', 'version' => '1.104.0', 'date' => '2026-11-06', 'title' => 'Stock control: every inventory movement carries a typed reason — in: PO receipt, manual entry, return from project, return from customer; out: delivery note to customer, delivery to production / project, consumption (consumables), issue on requisition, manual, scrap — with the document reference and the customer organisation; consumable items book their issues as consumption. Low-stock alarm per part (tick, minimum, reorder quantity; Procurement notified once a day when a part falls below), Inventory › Shortages console (free vs minimum, incoming from open orders and stock requisitions, gap, suggested order) raising one stock requisition on the Stock project; Settings › Procurement chooses or creates the Stock project.', 'db' => 'install/migrate_cp_r87_001_stock_control.sql', 'check' => 'r87a'],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R86-003', 'version' => '1.103.1', 'date' => '2026-11-06', 'title' => 'Requisition lines: the item box opens a drop-down of the recently requested / moved items on click, searches the inventory as you type, and (for Procurement) offers "➕ New inventory item" created when the line is saved; the Service (0.6.19), Golden PM (1.0.11) and Golden HR (1.0.5) apps show the recent items when the box is tapped.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R86-002', 'version' => '1.103.0', 'date' => '2026-11-06', 'title' => 'Purchase order / RFQ lines: the item box opens a drop-down of the supplier\'s items on click (bought before, preferred, or of a maker it represents), searches the whole inventory as you type, and offers "➕ New inventory item" — the item is created when the line is saved (code suggested from maker + part no., category, linked to the supplier); the maker is offered from the supplier\'s makers and the part no. from the item\'s codes (maker part no., barcode, code). Fix: the inline scripts and confirmations of the requisition, purchase order, BOM and payables pages were blocked by the Content-Security-Policy in browsers (no nonce) — pickers, filters, selection buttons and the "are you sure" questions did not run; all moved to nonce-tagged scripts and data-confirm / data-prompt.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R86-001', 'version' => '1.102.1', 'date' => '2026-11-06', 'title' => 'Procurement module end-to-end test (308 automated checks across requisitions, RFQ / PO, receipts and NCR, logistics, payables, BOM, inventory, apps API, five languages, three roles) — seven corrections: on a sent RFQ the line-delete buttons were nested inside the quotation form and could delete a line when saving prices; rejected goods (NCR replacement) could not be received again; cancelling a partially received order cancelled everything (now only the open balance, the order stays received); a requisition could be cancelled after goods were issued; a service report could push stock below zero silently (Procurement is now notified); four event labels missing in the PO log; a PHP warning after the supplier import. Over-budget approval now says why a note is needed.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R85-004', 'version' => '1.102.0', 'date' => '2026-11-06', 'title' => 'Organisations, step 3 (last): the customer import (Settings › Import › Customers) recognises a customer by VAT first, then ERP code, and creates or completes the organisation behind every imported customer (Customer role, master data); the related companies of a vessel (owner, manager, yard, class, agent, contractor, charterer) are organisations of the Contacts module instead of customer records — picked from the organisations, shown with their role pills, listed back on the organisation card; old rows are carried over.', 'db' => 'install/migrate_cp_r85_004_vessel_orgs.sql', 'check' => 'r85c'],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R85-003', 'version' => '1.101.1', 'date' => '2026-11-06', 'title' => 'Organisations are recognised by VAT number only: the Organisations page proposes links and duplicates by VAT, the supplier import matches an existing organisation by VAT (then by the ERP\'s own code, never by name), the Customer role links an existing customer by VAT — ERP code and name never match (two legal entities may share a name; one VAT is one entity).', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R85-002', 'version' => '1.101.0', 'date' => '2026-11-06', 'title' => 'Organisations, step 2: roles instead of a single kind — an organisation is ticked Customer · Supplier · Owner · Management · Yard · Class · Agent · Broker · Consultant at once; VAT, ERP code, address and postal code live on the organisation. The ★ Customer role creates or updates the billing record (projects, vessels, logins keep working) and the Supplier role opens the supplier card — both kept in step on every save, in either direction. A person may belong to several organisations (main one plus "Also belongs to"); supplier people, the e-mail card and the Contacts filters follow all memberships. Settings › Customers gets "New customer" = organisation with the Customer role.', 'db' => 'install/migrate_cp_r85_002_org_roles.sql', 'check' => 'r85b'],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R85-001', 'version' => '1.100.0', 'date' => '2026-11-06', 'title' => 'Organisations (option A, step 1): one register behind customers, companies and suppliers. Contacts gains the Suppliers button and the 🏛 Organisations page — every billing customer linked to its company of the Contacts module (matched by VAT, ERP code or name, confirmed one by one or all at once; master data completed both ways; the company created from the customer when none exists), duplicate companies merged (people, orders, invoices, prices, makers and the supplier card move, the duplicate is retired), people completed with the customer of their organisation. The person form creates a new organisation inline; Companies shows the ★ Customer and Supplier roles.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R84-003', 'version' => '1.99.2', 'date' => '2026-11-06', 'title' => 'A company can be a customer / owner / yard and a supplier at once: independent "supplier" flag on the company (Contacts › Companies: "Also a supplier" tick, ★ filter, gold pill linking to the supplier card); the supplier list, the ERP import and the purchase orders use the flag, and never change the kind of an existing company.', 'db' => 'install/migrate_cp_r84_003_is_supplier.sql', 'check' => 'r84c'],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R84-002', 'version' => '1.99.1', 'date' => '2026-11-06', 'title' => 'Suppliers › Import from ERP: a company already in the Contacts module under another kind (the name is unique) is matched by VAT, code or name and becomes a supplier instead of failing the whole import; a row that cannot be saved is reported and the rest go through.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R84-001', 'version' => '1.99.0', 'date' => '2026-11-06', 'title' => 'Procurement e-mail: five supplier templates (request for quotation, purchase order, expediting, non-conformance, remittance advice) under Settings › E-mail templates, chosen inside the ✉ card of the order / RFQ and of the paid supplier invoice; every ✉ card finds any person of the Contacts module by name, e-mail or company and adds him to the recipients. Suppliers › Import from ERP: downloadable template (sheets Suppliers + Contacts); the Contacts sheet creates or updates the people of each supplier in the Contacts module (category Supplier), so they are offered in the e-mail card; the supplier card lists its people with e-mail and phone.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R83-001', 'version' => '1.98.0', 'date' => '2026-11-06', 'title' => 'HR › Utilization: hours on projects against the working time of every portal user — capacity from the working calendar while employed, project hours from the timesheets, internal work and absences from the planning board, idle hours and whole idle days computed day by day; per month, per project and per activity for one person, team table per year or any period with discipline and technical-only filters, CSV and print; for HR, management, administrators and the managers of a discipline.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
