        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R72-003', 'version' => '1.80.7', 'date' => '2026-11-01', 'title' => 'Store builds: "Add this device" / passkey sign-in in the installed apps failed with "requestJson is required" — the native passkey plug-in takes the options as a JSON string (its JavaScript wrapper is not loaded by the shells); the three clients now call it that way (Service 0.6.7, Golden PM 1.0.5, Customer 1.0.4).', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R72-002', 'version' => '1.80.6', 'date' => '2026-11-01', 'title' => 'Golden PM 1.0.4 / Service 0.6.6: a message to HR sent from the app by someone who holds the HR or owner role was refused ("Not found") because the portal treated it as HR writing to a person — it now goes to the sender\'s own thread; queued HR operations show their text instead of raw data, and a rejected one shows the reason with a Discard button. Golden PM: the project search filters the list in place (the full re-render under a moving finger opened the first project by itself). Golden PM: Offers of the sub-project with number, revision, title, status, sent / valid-until dates and who decided — no amounts.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R72-001', 'version' => '1.80.5', 'date' => '2026-11-01', 'title' => 'Public privacy policy page (?p=privacy, no sign-in) for the portal and the three mobile apps — required by Google Play and the App Store; house style, English.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R71-005', 'version' => '1.80.4', 'date' => '2026-11-01', 'title' => 'Settings › Login history: saving the Android app-signing SHA-256 was blocked by the website firewall (a long hex string in a POST looks like an exploit) — the form now sends it encoded and the portal normalises it (colons optional, upper-case, 64 hex digits each).', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R71-004', 'version' => '1.80.3', 'date' => '2026-11-01', 'title' => 'Login page: "Sign in with a passkey" was rendered outside the white card, navy on the navy backdrop — invisible; it now sits inside the card under Sign in, with the house secondary-button style.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R71-003', 'version' => '1.80.2', 'date' => '2026-11-01', 'title' => 'Native passkeys for the store builds: the Capacitor shells move to Capacitor 8 with the @capgo/capacitor-passkey plug-in (same relying party goldensas.com, so a passkey made in Safari / Chrome works in the app and vice versa); the three clients use the native API when present (Service 0.6.5, Golden PM 1.0.3, Customer 1.0.3); one-time setup: mobile-native/wellknown.js writes the apple-app-site-association and assetlinks.json files for public_html/.well-known/, and Settings › Login history › "Android app signing SHA-256" lets the portal accept the Android app origin. npm audit of the shells: 0 vulnerabilities (was 17). Diagnostics: vessels already folded into a master are no longer reported as duplicates, and the remedy names Settings › Vessel duplicates.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R71-002', 'version' => '1.80.1', 'date' => '2026-11-01', 'title' => 'Passkeys: the "Sign in with a passkey" button failed with the browser message "A request is already pending" because the silent autofill request of the login page was still open — the button now cancels it first (AbortController), then asks for the passkey.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R71-001', 'version' => '1.80.0', 'date' => '2026-11-01', 'title' => 'Passkeys (WebAuthn / FIDO2): sign in to the portal and the three mobile apps with Face ID, Touch ID, fingerprint or Windows Hello instead of password + authenticator code — also after a sign-out. My Account › Passkeys: add this device (fresh authenticator code required when the account has one), list, remove; the login page offers "Sign in with a passkey" and the browser autofill; Settings › Login history: allow / forbid passkeys, every passkey of the portal with remove; notifications on add / remove; sign-in outcomes passkey / passkey_failed / passkey_added / passkey_removed. Mobile API: /auth/passkey/options + /auth/passkey/login, /me/passkeys. Verification in-house (no library): origin and rpId checks, user verification required, single-use 5-minute challenges, signature-counter regression refused and reported, 10 attempts per address per 10 minutes, at most 10 passkeys per account. Apps: Service 0.6.4, Golden PM 1.0.2, Customer 1.0.2. Security review docs/SECURITY-REVIEW_R71-001.md.', 'db' => 'install/migrate_cp_r71_passkeys.sql', 'check' => 'r71'],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R70-005', 'version' => '1.79.9', 'date' => '2026-11-01', 'title' => 'Mobile apps — Lock with Face ID (Service 0.6.3, Golden PM 1.0.1, Customer 1.0.1): More › 🔒 Lock app keeps the session on the phone and Face ID / fingerprint opens it again; a cancelled prompt returns to the lock screen instead of signing out (Golden PM used to sign out); the Service app gains the "Face ID on open" setting; the login screen explains that Unlock is available after one password sign-in on the device. Sign out remains the full revoke.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R70-004', 'version' => '1.79.8', 'date' => '2026-11-01', 'title' => 'World clocks per user: My Account › World clocks — tick up to 7 zones from a catalogue of 34 yachting and business places (Monaco, Barcelona, Split, Tivat, Fort Lauderdale, Singapore …); UTC is always first for everybody; Reset returns to the company set. Fix: the HR requests page died at the bottom (training applications box called two functions that did not exist), which also left the clock strip at --:-- and the pickers dead on that page. Fix: the monthly KPI snapshot (first page of each month) broke after the first project with a KPI drop (a variable clash) and took the dashboard down for the first visitor of the month; it now resumes project by project and completes.', 'db' => 'install/migrate_cp_r70_clocks.sql', 'check' => 'r70d'],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R70-003', 'version' => '1.79.7', 'date' => '2026-11-01', 'title' => 'Community: @mentions in post comments and post bodies — type @ and pick a colleague (same picker as notes and ticket comments), the handle is highlighted in the thread and the colleague is notified ("… mentioned you in Community · <post>"); the post author still receives the usual comment notice.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R70-002', 'version' => '1.79.6', 'date' => '2026-11-01', 'title' => 'Community: the kind selector and the photo field work again — four inline scripts (Community compose, Targets scope ×2, Training target) carried no Content-Security-Policy nonce and were blocked by the browser, so the photo field never appeared and the scope / target selectors did not switch. A photo (jpg / png / webp up to 12 MB) can now accompany any post or poll, not only the photo kind; an oversized upload says so instead of "choose a photo".', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R70-001', 'version' => '1.79.5', 'date' => '2026-10-31', 'title' => 'Store builds from GitHub: Actions › Build Android app (signed App Bundle → artifact → Play Console track) and Build iOS app (macOS runner, archive → IPA → TestFlight) for the three apps from mobile-native/ (Capacitor shells of customer/mobile, mobile-pm, mobile-customer; icons and splash generated from the clients\' icons; setup of the Apple / Google accounts and secrets in mobile-native/README.md). The three app folders answer at their short URL (DirectoryIndex).', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R69-002', 'version' => '1.79.4', 'date' => '2026-10-31', 'title' => 'Performance pass, no functional change: a short-lived block cache (APCu or storage/cache) keeps the menu counters (45 s per user, dropped on every action), the online list (20 s / 60 s) and the dashboard fleet, activity and celebration cards (10 min per language); 21 indexes on the tables behind the dashboard counters, the activity ranking and the HR balances; presence heartbeat every 2 min (online window 5 min); a daily house-keeping run on the first page of each day (read notifications older than 90 days, sign-in log older than a year, assistant log older than 180 days, sent push items older than 30 days, session files older than 7 days, update backups beyond the last 3, oversized logs trimmed); a query meter in the footer for administrators (queries · ms) with a slow-pages log (over 2 s or 150 queries) shown in Diagnostics together with the cache state and the last house-keeping; Flush cache and Clear slow-pages log buttons.', 'db' => 'install/migrate_cp_r69_perf.sql', 'check' => 'r69b'],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R69-001', 'version' => '1.79.3', 'date' => '2026-10-31', 'title' => 'Settings › About › Diagnostics: one click runs read-only checks of the database (queries running now, open transactions and locks, connections, table health, missing database steps, orphan references, duplicates, growing tables, backlog) and of the application (PHP version and limits, extensions, storage folders, disk, session files, update lock, configuration, assistant reachability, timings of the heaviest pages, the PHP error log) — each with OK / warn / fail and what to do; report download; the portal now writes PHP errors to storage/php-errors.log.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R67-002', 'version' => '1.79.2', 'date' => '2026-10-31', 'title' => 'HR Assistant: an AMKA whose first six digits differ from the date of birth is no longer refused — the AMKA is issued from the registration certificate, which may carry a later date. The employee ticks "My AMKA was issued with this date", the value is staged with a note that HR sees next to the field on the review ("AMKA date differs from the date of birth — confirmed by the employee"); the digits must still form a date (DDMMYY). Manuals and the five languages updated.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R64-007', 'version' => '1.79.1', 'date' => '2026-10-31', 'title' => 'Settings › Disciplines: one structure, no duplicates — each row now shows portal accounts and 🪪 employee cards, and "Merge into…" moves every account, card, target, leave period and training of a duplicate into the discipline you choose and deletes it. The people import no longer creates departments on its own: unknown names are matched loosely (case, accents, the word "department" ignored) and otherwise the card keeps its department unless HR ticks "create unknown departments".', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R68-001', 'version' => '1.79.0', 'date' => '2026-10-31', 'title' => 'Customer app 1.0.0 — the portal on a phone for owners\' representatives, captains and yard PMs (customer/mobile-customer/, third application of the mobile API customer/api/v1 with X-App "customer"; sign-in limited to customer accounts, staff tokens never served). Home / Action Centre with the items waiting for the customer; service reports (SF-GLD-014) read in the app and accepted with a drawn signature and the acceptance statement — or sent back with a remark — through the portal\'s own fsr_customer_decide (the web page uses the same function; the signature image is filed as fsr_sign); documents submitted for Owner approval decided A / B (note required) / D (note required) through oa_decide with the comment thread; offers sent for decision accepted (signature + statement, refused once the validity date has passed) or rejected with a note through of_decide; tickets with the external thread only (internal notes never leave), replies with photos and files through tk_comment / tk_store_uploads, close a resolved ticket, re-open, new ticket; vessels, project progress (4-stage line), documents shared with the customer. Device biometric unlock on the phone; decisions ask for the authenticator code when the account has 2FA (same step-up as Golden PM), and decisions on offers from the app require 2FA on the customer account (setting api_customer_offer_2fa, default on). The drawn signatures are printed inside the acceptance boxes of the service report PDF (engineer and customer). Settings › Login history › Mobile apps: minimum version of the customer app; Portal accounts › ⎋ Revoke device also for customer accounts; Account › Devices in the app. Five languages. Security review CS-36 … CS-42.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R67-001', 'version' => '1.78.0', 'date' => '2026-10-31', 'title' => 'HR Assistant (HR › HR Assistant): guided, step-by-step flows with a staging area approved by HR — first flow "My card": every employee with a card completes or corrects his own personal data (identity and family, contact and address, identification numbers and bank, education and work, documents, review and declaration), pre-filled with what the card holds, validated at entry (AMKA against the date of birth, ΑΦΜ check digit, IBAN, plausible dates); the assistant proposes values from free text or from a photo of the ID / passport (suggestions only, confirmed field by field); authenticator code on the identification step and on submission for accounts with 2FA; GDPR notice accepted and logged; HR reviews the field-by-field diff, approves or rejects per field, returns for corrections or approves & applies — the values go through the normal card save with the change log, the documents are filed on the card, the employee is notified. Staged identification numbers are encrypted at rest (libsodium), staged data is purged 90 days after the decision, reminders for idle drafts and waiting submissions. Flow templates per branch in HR › HR Assistant › Flow templates; the engine carries the hiring, leaving and dismissal flows of R67-002 / R67-003. Card completeness and the start button on My leave, open-flow banner on the employee card, pending flows on the HR dashboard, nav badge for HR.', 'db' => 'install/migrate_cp_r67_hr_assistant.sql', 'check' => 'r67'],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R66-001', 'version' => '1.77.0', 'date' => '2026-10-31', 'title' => 'Golden PM app 1.0.0 — the mobile API (customer/api/v1) serves a second application for project managers and managers (X-App: pm; sign-in limited to staff who are a PM, an HR manager, a timesheet approver or an administrator). Read model GET /pm/projects (project tree with the 7-stage percentages, fed stages, teams, overdue drawings, open submittals and issues), /pm/subproject/{id} (issues, comments, team notes, drawings, submittals, budgets as hours, team, who is away), /pm/drawings, /pm/submittals, /pm/hr/team (people I approve for with annual balance, requests to decide, timesheets to approve, 28-day absence matrix of codes only), /pm/absences, /pm/inbox. Sync kinds sp_stages (pct columns only, fed stages ignored, snapshot + invoicing follow-ups as the portal), sp_comment, issue_status, drawing_update, hr_decide (manager stage only, authenticator code when the account has 2FA, logged with "(mobile app)"), ts_decide (same step-up), nf_read. Monetary and personal / payroll data never leave; HR-stage decisions and engineering extra-hours decisions stay in the portal. Settings › Log › Mobile apps sets the minimum version of each app separately.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R65-003', 'version' => '1.76.5', 'date' => '2026-10-31', 'title' => 'Service Engineer app 0.6.2: Ukrainian and Bulgarian translations completed (the app had only the tabs and the sign-in screen in these languages and showed everything else in English), Greek and Italian completed to the full set; the remaining English labels of the equipment detail, the queue and the report header follow the chosen language. Client only, no API change.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R64-006', 'version' => '1.76.4', 'date' => '2026-10-31', 'title' => 'Early leaves / late arrivals (and every hour type that consumes annual leave) accumulate: only each completed 8 hours takes one day of annual leave; the remaining hours are shown on My leave under the annual balance ("4 h accumulated · 4 h to the next day") instead of charging fractions of a day.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R64-005', 'version' => '1.76.3', 'date' => '2026-10-31', 'title' => 'Settings › Portal accounts: a deactivated account with no history at all (no sign-ins, tickets, timesheets, reports, planning, employee card, approvals, requests, community) can be deleted for good (🗑 next to Enable); any account with history is deactivated, never deleted, and the portal says what keeps it.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R64-004', 'version' => '1.76.2', 'date' => '2026-10-31', 'title' => 'People import: a column that is not in the file never touches the card — prior service, working days, children, technical flag, contract type / part-time and every personal field keep their values (the previous import wrote 0 / defaults / empty for absent columns). The preview shows "=" where the card keeps its value. Workbook GAS-HR-restore-import.xlsx restores technical / working days / children / prior service from the earlier imports.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R65-002', 'version' => '1.76.1', 'date' => '2026-10-31', 'title' => 'Service Engineer app 0.6.1: the sign-in screen now asks for the authenticator code when the account has two-factor authentication (the portal\'s reply was not recognised and showed "Sign in failed"); a wrong code and a non-staff account get their own messages.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R65-001', 'version' => '1.76.0', 'date' => '2026-10-31', 'title' => 'Service Engineer app build 0.6.0 — My HR page in the app (= HR › My leave): balances per leave type from the entitlement engine, leave periods to join with own dates, new leave request for every type enabled for the person (day / hour, reason and document rules; a document is sent as a PDF or photo), own requests with the manager\'s and HR\'s decisions and cancel while pending, training opportunities with apply and own trainings, annual evaluations with acknowledge and comment, private messages with HR (unread badge on Home and More). The mobile API (customer/api/v1) gains GET /hr, POST /hr/request, GET /hr/doc/{id} and the sync kinds hr_request, hr_cancel, hr_period_join, hr_training_apply, hr_eval_ack, hr_message, hr_seen — every write goes through the portal\'s own HR functions, decisions stay in the portal (hr_decide → 403), only the person\'s own records are readable, personal and payroll data are never read. Every engineer needs a person card linked to his portal account (HR › People).', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R64-003', 'version' => '1.75.2', 'date' => '2026-10-31', 'title' => 'People Excel: the pre-filled template exports every card field as stored; the personal / payroll columns are included only for HR and Owner accounts (as on the card), and the import preview warns when a file carries personal columns the signed-in account cannot write (they are skipped, the rest of the row is imported). Empty cells never erase data.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R64-002', 'version' => '1.75.1', 'date' => '2026-10-31', 'title' => 'Assistant on evaluations and targets: on the evaluation panel (card and manager page) "Draft the evaluation" fills the eight scores and the texts from the facts of the year — trainings, computed scores, targets, last evaluation, portal activity, kudos — for review before saving, and "Ask" answers questions about the person\'s year; on HR › Targets "Propose" returns 4–6 SMART targets for a department or a person (from its people and roles, last year\'s targets and results, the evaluation) to add with one click or edit first. Personal and payroll data are never sent. Pages hr_eval and hr_targets must be enabled under Settings › Assistant › Pages.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R64-001', 'version' => '1.75.0', 'date' => '2026-10-31', 'title' => 'Personal and payroll data visible to HR and Owner only (plain administrators no longer see or import them). The Owner is excluded from the activity rankings, the most-active lists and the winner of the month. Who is online: a drop-down on the topbar with the names and the time online; full table with sign-in time, uptime and last activity on My Account. Annual evaluation gains two computed criteria — training participation (ranked among colleagues) and attendance & consistency (early leaves / late arrivals, unplanned absences, last-moment requests) — included in the overall score; "How we evaluate you" on My leave explains the eight criteria, the computed scores, the targets and shows each person his computed scores so far, plus a note from HR. Targets for the company, departments and individuals (HR › Targets; managers for their people): measure, target value, due date, weight, progress and status with history; everybody sees the targets that concern him on My leave and updates his own progress; achievement is summarised in the evaluation.', 'db' => 'install/migrate_cp_r64_targets.sql', 'check' => 'r64'],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R63-003', 'version' => '1.74.1', 'date' => '2026-10-31', 'title' => 'Two new manual editions under Support: the HR Manager Handbook (people register and card, imports, leave engine, requests, periods and closures, training, evaluations, off-boarding, the 1 January checklist, Community tools, data protection — HR / Owner / administrators) and the Employee Guide (balances, requesting leave, periods, my program, trainings and certificates, my evaluation, messages with HR, Community — every Golden A/S account). Both are searched by the help search.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R63-001', 'version' => '1.74.0', 'date' => '2026-10-31', 'title' => 'Community: wishes on birthdays, name days, work anniversaries and new colleagues (one click from the dashboard, wishes wall for the person); kudos between colleagues with most-thanked lists; noticeboard with posts, polls and photos (reactions, comments, pinning); automatic badges; winner of the month with prize; onboarding checklist with a buddy; morning celebration nudge and Monday digest in Notifications. New page Community (🤝).', 'db' => 'install/migrate_cp_r63_social.sql', 'check' => 'r63'],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R62-006', 'version' => '1.73.5', 'date' => '2026-10-30', 'title' => 'Dark mode: navy text (planning board headers and day numbers, discipline group rows, tab titles, section headings, pill labels) turns light on the dark background; planning board name and header columns get a solid dark background.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R62-005', 'version' => '1.73.4', 'date' => '2026-10-30', 'title' => 'Dashboard › Fleet & activity: vessels worked on this year and in the last 30 days, new vessels of the year, active vessels; the ten most active colleagues of the year and of the last 30 days (records created across the portal, with the breakdown on hover and the timesheet hours).', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R62-004', 'version' => '1.73.3', 'date' => '2026-10-30', 'title' => 'Celebrations: staff dashboard shows birthdays and Greek Orthodox name days of colleagues for the next 14 days (no ages); the HR dashboard shows 30 days with the age and a link to the card. Name days include the movable feasts (Easter, St George, St Thomas, Ψυχοσάββατο …).', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R62-003', 'version' => '1.73.2', 'date' => '2026-10-30', 'title' => 'Leave days never include weekends and public holidays: a work calendar without weekday rules now has Saturday / Sunday off, and a year whose holidays were not generated falls back to the country\'s public holidays (Greek Orthodox Easter included). HR › Leaves › leave periods: "Recount days" fixes already assigned periods and rewrites the board.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R62-002', 'version' => '1.73.1', 'date' => '2026-10-30', 'title' => 'HR is its own group in the left menu (HR dashboard, My leave, HR requests, Leaves, Training, HR settings) between Work and Commercial — Work keeps tickets, work orders, reports, timesheets, planning, tasks.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R62-001', 'version' => '1.73.0', 'date' => '2026-10-30', 'title' => 'Employee card carries the full payroll record (father\'s / mother\'s / spouse name, nationality, birth place, passport, blood group, education, grade, transport, work phone and extension, postcode, city, country, gross salary, ΟΑΕΔ benefit, payroll code — masked where sensitive, importable from the people Excel). Mandatory company-closure leave periods (HR assigns to everybody; staff cannot opt out). HR › Training: introductory, internal and external trainings published by HR with target, places and apply-by date; staff apply from My leave, manager or HR approves; attendance, result and certificate (number, validity, scan) kept on the card › Training; expiring certificates on the HR dashboard. Annual evaluations (8 criteria 1–5, overall, strengths, improvements, goals, training needs; draft → final → acknowledged by the employee with comment) with evolution chart and participation summary on the card › Evaluations.', 'db' => 'install/migrate_cp_r62_training_eval.sql', 'check' => 'r62'],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R61-001', 'version' => '1.72.0', 'date' => '2026-10-30', 'title' => 'Owner role (scope "Owner": full portal plus every HR page and record without administrator rights). HR › Leaves: who is away over any period for the whole company or one discipline (day matrix, totals per type), leave periods / groups HR publishes per year for the company, disciplines or named people — staff join from My leave with their own dates inside the period, the manager approves and the leave is assigned automatically; HR can also assign a period to everyone at once and undo it; optional cap on participants. Assistant question box on the Leaves page (answers from the period shown).', 'db' => 'install/migrate_cp_r61_owner_leaves.sql', 'check' => 'r61'],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R60-007', 'version' => '1.71.0', 'date' => '2026-10-30', 'title' => 'Personal data on the employee card (HR and administrators only): personal e-mail, mobile and home phone, home address, date of birth, AMKA, VAT number (ΑΦΜ) and tax office, ID / passport number, IBAN and bank, emergency contact — validated (AMKA 11 digits, ΑΦΜ 9 digits, IBAN check digits), masked in the change log, and importable / exportable through the people Excel template.', 'db' => 'install/migrate_cp_r60_007_personal_data.sql', 'check' => 'r60c'],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R60-004', 'version' => '1.70.0', 'date' => '2026-10-30', 'title' => 'Balance import as a cut-over: the imported sheet is the truth "as of" a date (Settings › HR › Import balances › Balances as of) — the entitlement, carry-over and taken days of the sheet are fixed (🔓) and only requests and board entries after that date count, so leave records imported for the same year are no longer added on top (negative balances). Earlier records stay in the history and on the board.', 'db' => 'install/migrate_cp_r60_004_counted_from.sql', 'check' => 'r60b'],
        ['ref' => 'GAS-CP-R60-006', 'version' => '1.69.6', 'date' => '2026-10-30', 'title' => 'Settings › Portal accounts is fast again: the manager and customer lists of every row are filled only when a drop-down is opened (one copy of each list on the page instead of one per account), and the row drop-downs use the plain browser list — the Add account form keeps the type-to-search lists.', 'db' => null, 'check' => null],
